<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Mastieni</h1><p class="st-meta">600 BCE – 230 BCE (approx.) · capital Mastia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Iberian people of the Cartagena region, whose town Mastia marked the limit set on Roman shipping in a 4th-century BCE treaty with Carthage.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Mastieni lived in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, around modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthago-nova">Cartagena</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murcia">Murcia</a>. Greek writers knew them from the 6th century BCE, and they belonged to the Iberian culture of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Almost nothing is known of their institutions. Their chief town, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mastia">Mastia</a>, is named in the second treaty between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, of 348 BCE, as the point beyond which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> could not trade or found cities. The region was rich in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and lead, later intensively mined.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 227 BCE the Carthaginian general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasdrubal-the-fair">Hasdrubal</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthago-nova">Qart Hadasht</a>, later Carthago Nova, probably on or near the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mastia">Mastia</a>, making it the capital of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/barcid-iberia">Barcid Iberia</a>. The Mastieni name then disappears.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/mastieni.jpg" alt="Mastieni" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Nanosanchez · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cratera_museo_cartagena.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 BCE – 230 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mastia</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Iberian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Iberian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mastienoi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-415&amp;focus=mastieni" aria-label="Mastieni on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4601 718 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Mastieni lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4975 1081h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4921 974h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4921 974h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Spain. <a href="/atlas?year=-415&amp;focus=mastieni">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

